  <section style="background:var(--white);padding:2rem 0 3rem;">
    <div class="blog-post">
      <div class="blog-body">
        <p><strong>We do not offer ECO4, grants or funded boilers. We do not install under the scheme. This guide explains how ECO4 works, so you know where to start.</strong></p>

        <h2>What Is the ECO4 Scheme?</h2>
        <p>ECO4 stands for Energy Company Obligation 4. It is a government scheme. Large energy firms must pay for energy saving work in some homes. If you qualify, this can mean a new boiler, first-time central heating or insulation at no cost to you.</p>
        <p><a href="https://www.ofgem.gov.uk/faqs-domestic-consumers-and-landlords" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Ofgem</a> runs the scheme. It started in 2022. It is aimed at the least efficient homes and people most at risk of fuel poverty. The end date and rules have changed over time, and may change again. Check the latest rules on GOV.UK or with Ofgem before you apply.</p>

        <div class="blog-callout">
          <strong>ECO4 funding is limited</strong>
          <p>Energy firms have set budgets for ECO4. Funding may run out, or the scheme may close. If you think you qualify, check soon. Always check the latest rules on GOV.UK first.</p>
        </div>
        <CallStrip inline title="Not eligible, or need a boiler now?" text="New boilers from £2,195 fitted, with a fixed written price." />

        <h2>Who Qualifies for ECO4 in Liverpool?</h2>
        <p>There are two main tests. Your income or benefits. And how energy efficient your home is.</p>

        <h3>Income and benefit eligibility</h3>
        <p>You usually need to get at least one of these benefits:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Universal Credit</li>
          <li>Pension Credit (Guarantee or Savings Credit)</li>
          <li>Housing Benefit</li>
          <li>Income-based Jobseeker's Allowance (JSA)</li>
          <li>Income-related Employment and Support Allowance (ESA)</li>
          <li>Income Support</li>
          <li>Child Benefit (subject to an income limit)</li>
        </ul>
        <p>This list can change. Check the latest list on GOV.UK or with your energy supplier.</p>

        <h3>Property energy efficiency</h3>
        <p>Your home's EPC (Energy Performance Certificate) rating usually needs to be D, E, F or G. Homes rated A, B or C are seen as efficient enough. You can check your rating for free with the <a href="https://www.gov.uk/find-energy-certificate" target="_blank" rel="noopener">GOV.UK EPC checker</a>. If your home has no EPC, one can be done as part of the ECO4 checks.</p>

        <h3>ECO4 Flex: if you do not receive qualifying benefits</h3>
        <p>You may still qualify without these benefits. This is called ECO4 Flex. It is for homes on a low income, or where a health condition is made worse by a cold home. Your council can refer you if you meet its own rules. Contact <a href="https://liverpool.gov.uk" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Liverpool City Council</a> to ask if you might qualify.</p>

        <h2>What Can ECO4 Fund in Liverpool?</h2>
        <p>ECO4 looks at the whole house, not just the boiler. An assessor works out which mix of work makes the biggest difference. This can include:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Swapping an old boiler for a new, efficient condensing boiler</li>
          <li>First-time central heating in a home with none</li>
          <li>Loft insulation</li>
          <li>Cavity wall insulation, where the cavity is empty</li>
          <li>Solid wall insulation, inside or out, for older homes with no cavity</li>
          <li>Smart heating controls as part of a wider upgrade</li>
        </ul>
        <p>Not every home gets every measure. The assessor surveys your home and decides what is needed.</p>

        <h2>What ECO4 Does Not Cover</h2>
        <p>ECO4 is about making homes more efficient. It does not pay for:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Boiler repairs or servicing (it pays for upgrades, not upkeep)</li>
          <li>Homes that already meet the energy rating it is aiming for</li>
        </ul>
        <p>There is a separate grant for heat pumps called the <a href="https://www.gov.uk/apply-boiler-upgrade-scheme" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Boiler Upgrade Scheme</a>. Check GOV.UK for who it is open to.</p>

        <h2>How to Apply for ECO4 in Liverpool</h2>
        <p>There is no single government form. Approved installers deliver ECO4 using energy firm budgets. These steps will help you start:</p>
        <ol>
          <li>Check your EPC rating at <a href="https://www.gov.uk/find-energy-certificate" target="_blank" rel="noopener">gov.uk/check-energy-performance-certificate</a></li>
          <li>Check you get a qualifying benefit, or ask Liverpool City Council about Flex</li>
          <li>Ask your energy supplier or the council about ECO4. Ofgem has guidance for households</li>
          <li>If you qualify, an approved assessor visits to confirm what work is needed</li>
          <li>Approved installers then do the work, at no cost to you</li>
        </ol>

        <h2>What Happens After ECO4? The Warm Homes Plan</h2>
        <p>The government has announced the Warm Homes Plan. It is meant to help improve the least efficient homes, with insulation, low-carbon heating and smart controls. Some Warm Homes grants are already running in some areas. Details and dates may change. Check the latest guidance on <a href="https://www.gov.uk/apply-great-british-insulation-scheme" target="_blank" rel="noopener">GOV.UK</a>.</p>

        <div class="blog-success">
          <strong>Not eligible for ECO4?</strong>
          <p>If you are paying for a new boiler yourself, <a href="/boiler-installation-liverpool" style="color:#15803d;">see our boiler installation page</a> for our standard prices. These are not grant-funded.</p>
        </div>
        <CallStrip inline title="Want us to take a look?" text="Call for advice or a price. Gas Safe registered, no call-out fee." />

        <h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
        <div class="pf-faq">
          <details class="pf-faq-item"><summary><span class="pf-faq-tag pf-tag-green">ELIGIBLE</span><span class="pf-faq-q">How do I know if I qualify for ECO4 in Liverpool?</span></summary><div class="pf-faq-body"><p>You usually need a qualifying benefit, such as Universal Credit, Pension Credit or Housing Benefit. Your home usually needs an EPC rating of D, E, F or G. Check your EPC for free at gov.uk/check-energy-performance-certificate. Your energy supplier or Liverpool City Council can confirm if you qualify. We do not offer ECO4 ourselves.</p></div></details>
          <details class="pf-faq-item"><summary><span class="pf-faq-tag pf-tag-navy">FREE</span><span class="pf-faq-q">Is a new boiler completely free under ECO4?</span></summary><div class="pf-faq-body"><p>For homes that qualify, it usually is. The energy firm pays for the boiler, fitting, controls and any insulation needed. Some complex jobs may need a small payment from you. The installer should confirm this before any work is agreed.</p></div></details>
          <details class="pf-faq-item"><summary><span class="pf-faq-tag pf-tag-orange">TENANT</span><span class="pf-faq-q">Can tenants apply for ECO4 funding in Liverpool?</span></summary><div class="pf-faq-body"><p>Yes, private tenants can apply. It is the tenant's benefits that count, not the landlord's. The landlord must agree to the work in writing. Rules for rented homes can differ, so check GOV.UK or with your energy supplier.</p></div></details>
          <details class="pf-faq-item"><summary><span class="pf-faq-tag pf-tag-navy">DEADLINE</span><span class="pf-faq-q">When does ECO4 end?</span></summary><div class="pf-faq-body"><p>The end date has changed before and could change again. Check the latest rules on GOV.UK or with Ofgem. Funding is limited, so if you think you qualify, check soon. The Warm Homes Plan is expected to follow ECO4.</p></div></details>
          <details class="pf-faq-item"><summary><span class="pf-faq-tag pf-tag-orange">FLEX</span><span class="pf-faq-q">What is ECO4 Flex and do I need qualifying benefits?</span></summary><div class="pf-faq-body"><p>No, not with Flex. ECO4 Flex lets councils refer homes that do not get a qualifying benefit. You need to meet the council's own rules on low income or health. Contact Liverpool City Council to ask if you might qualify.</p></div></details>
        </div>
      </div>

